{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530681-m20-sphere-needed-for-effects","id":1530681,"title":"M20 Sphere needed for effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-12T16:11:18-08:00","id":1530681,"title":"M20 Sphere needed for effects","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have many questions about which spheres and what levels are needed for some effects:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Entropy 4 can cause aggravated damage</b>. To whom? Do I need Matter to harm Vampires? Mind to harm Fae? Spirit for Werewolves? Essentially, does Entropy 4 on its own suffice to harm a creature/object or do I need other spheres?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 can harm material objects</b>. Do Vampires count as objects for this damage?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 can bless/curse.</b> Does it need other spheres to affect things and living beings?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 / Prime 2 can harm ghosts</b>. Is the damage aggravated due to Prime? Does it cost Quintessence per attack?</li> <li><b>Prime 2 can make attacks do aggravated damage</b>, can it be any type of attack? Entropy 3 attack causing aggravated damage to things/people with just Prime 2?</li> <li><b>Prime 2 can make attacks do aggravated damage</b>, do I need Matter to enchant objects? (The write up mentions needing Life for living beings, but nothing for objects).</li> <li><s><b>Mind 3 / Prime 2 can deal aggravated damage.</b> Is this subject to the Willpower +X for other Mages and Night Folk?</s> Found the answer on HDYDT</li> </ol>Those are the main questions, but others might arise depending on the answers.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-15-2024, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T19:13:28-08:00","id":1530698,"title":"","content":"1) Good question. Entropy 4 directly attacks patterns, so it should be able to attack any pattern.<br /> <br /> 2) No, Vampires count as Life, they are just unusual enough that they need a Matter augment.<br /> <br /> 3) This is trickier. It should be capable of affecting predictable patterns on its own as that is one of its explicit capabilities. That\u2019s how I run it. That said M20 is inconsistent on this and you can probably find counter examples.<br /> <br /> 4) It\u2019s Aggravated, I think, because Entropy does bad, bad things to ghosts. I\u2019m not sure Mage Entropy should, but that\u2019s another discussion. It should not require quintessence because otherwise, what\u2019s the point? <br /> <br /> 5) Pretty much any attack, I think. Entropy 3 can\u2019t actually attack directly, though (other than ghosts apparently). <br /> <br /> 6) It shouldn\u2019t need either Life or Matter. I think in earlier drafts it was harder to affect Life than Matter but it was changed some time before release as it is not a rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T20:02:44-08:00","id":1530701,"title":"","content":"What I mean by that last one is that there is parity between Matter and Life. If a spell requires Life when cast on living things it should require Matter when cast on objects, and if it does not require Matter when cast on objects it should not require Life when cast on living creatures.<br /> <br /> Enchant Patterns and Enchant Life are explicitly abilities of Prime 2 and Prime 3 respectively so that\u2019s something they be able to do on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T05:59:03-08:00","id":1530736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530681-m20-sphere-needed-for-effects?p=1530698#post1530698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Good question. Entropy 4 directly attacks patterns, so it should be able to attack any pattern.<br /> <br /> 2) No, Vampires count as Life, they are just unusual enough that they need a Matter augment.<br /> <br /> 3) This is trickier. It should be capable of affecting predictable patterns on its own as that is one of its explicit capabilities. That\u2019s how I run it. That said M20 is inconsistent on this and you can probably find counter examples.<br /> <br /> 4) It\u2019s Aggravated, I think, because Entropy does bad, bad things to ghosts. I\u2019m not sure Mage Entropy should, but that\u2019s another discussion. It should not require quintessence because otherwise, what\u2019s the point?<br /> <br /> 5) Pretty much any attack, I think. Entropy 3 can\u2019t actually attack directly, though (other than ghosts apparently).<br /> <br /> 6) It shouldn\u2019t need either Life or Matter. I think in earlier drafts it was harder to affect Life than Matter but it was changed some time before release as it is not a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Fixed the question content 02-13-2024, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T19:36:49-08:00","id":1530773,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t see your question seven. I\u2019m glad you found an answer. I\u2019ll give mine anyways in case anyone else needs it.<br /> <br /> Even augmented by Prime 2 a Mind attack is still a Mind attack. So yes it is willpower +x difficulty, unless it is an attack on a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T21:03:49-08:00","id":1530865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530681-m20-sphere-needed-for-effects#post1530681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have many questions about which spheres and what levels are needed for some effects:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Entropy 4 can cause aggravated damage</b>. To whom? Do I need Matter to harm Vampires? Mind to harm Fae? Spirit for Werewolves? Essentially, does Entropy 4 on its own suffice to harm a creature/object or do I need other spheres?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 can harm material objects</b>. Do Vampires count as objects for this damage?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 can bless/curse.</b> Does it need other spheres to affect things and living beings?</li> <li><b>Entropy 3 / Prime 2 can harm ghosts</b>. Is the damage aggravated due to Prime? Does it cost Quintessence per attack?</li> <li><b>Prime 2 can make attacks do aggravated damage</b>, can it be any type of attack? Entropy 3 attack causing aggravated damage to things/people with just Prime 2?</li> <li><b>Prime 2 can make attacks do aggravated damage</b>, do I need Matter to enchant objects? (The write up mentions needing Life for living beings, but nothing for objects).</li> <li><u><b>Mind 3 / Prime 2 </b><b>can deal aggravated damage.</b> Is this subject to the Willpower +X for other Mages and Night Folk? </u>Found the answer on HDYDT</li> </ol>Those are the main questions, but others might arise depending on the answers.<br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>With regard to entropy 3/ prime 2/ the answer is that for some paradigms it does. For others, hell, possibly most, it is not the death sphere and ought never had been presented as such in the core rules...anyhow, an euthanatos, a void engineer can do it, a hermetic would need spirit rather than entropy, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T07:10:12-08:00","id":1530897,"title":"","content":"To split hairs: Entropy 3/Prime 2 can always hurt ghosts, but some paradigms simply won't use the ability. The game mechanics of Entropy haven't changed, they just don't come into play.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T19:20:28-08:00","id":1530943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530681-m20-sphere-needed-for-effects?p=1530897#post1530897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To split hairs: Entropy 3/Prime 2 can always hurt ghosts, but some paradigms simply won't use the ability. The game mechanics of Entropy haven't changed, they just don't come into play.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As of M20 this is probably correct. Still, to split atoms, i prefer to see the borders of the spheres as rather fluid. For instance, the sorcerer crusade has Entropy listed as Fate, and, if not mistaken, it lacks necromantic aspects (of course a heart attack is still a heart attack but ghosts is another thing entirely)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}